In `buildAuditRawText` (src/pipeline-self-audit.js), I added a `hasInconclusive` check using `tasks.some(t => t.reviewInconclusive === true)` that, when any cluster task carries the flag, overrides the fault-side note with the distinct string `'gate-inconclusive (stochastic re-roll, not a genuine reviewer rejection)'`. The non-inconclusive path still uses the original three `faultSideNote` entries unchanged. I also added 2 new test definitions to src/pipeline-self-audit.test.js (one asserting the new label appears, one asserting the original `Classified as:` wording is preserved when no task has the flag), bringing the file from 11 to 13 tests.

Acceptance:
1. `grep -n "gate-inconclusive (stochastic re-roll, not a genuine reviewer rejection)" src/pipeline-self-audit.js` returns a hit inside `buildAuditRawText` -- `grep -n ... src/pipeline-self-audit.js` -- PASS (line 103)
2. `grep -n "reviewInconclusive" src/pipeline-self-audit.js` returns at least one hit, appears only in the new conditional -- `grep -n ... src/pipeline-self-audit.js` -- PASS (line 101, single hit)
3. `node --test src/pipeline-self-audit.test.js` passes; test file contains assertion on the literal string AND a regression assertion -- `node --test src/pipeline-self-audit.test.js` -- PASS (13 tests, 0 fail; test 12 asserts the literal string, test 13 asserts `doesNotMatch /gate-inconclusive/` + `match /Classified as:/`)
4. Three existing `faultSideNote` map entries unmodified; `grep -c "faultSideNote"` is still 2 -- `grep -c "faultSideNote" src/pipeline-self-audit.js` -- PASS (returns 2)

